          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How many calories are in Transparent Labs Mass Gainer?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A full two-scoop serving has 750 to 770 calories, depending on flavor, per the labels at the time of writing: 770 for Chocolate Glaze and Chocolate Peanut Butter, 760 for Sweet Vanilla and 750 for Strawberry Cheesecake. Mixing it with 16 oz of whole milk instead of water adds roughly 300 calories, which brings a serving to around 1,070."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I take Transparent Labs Mass Gainer if I have diabetes or kidney disease?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Only with your doctor's approval. About 100 g of each serving is tapioca maltodextrin, which raises blood sugar quickly, and each serving adds 53 g of protein and 3 g of creatine, both of which matter for kidney disease. A doctor or registered dietitian can tell you whether a gainer, a smaller protein shake or food is the safer option."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: SITE_NAME, url: SITE_URL },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.brand ?? product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: author.name,
    section: "Brand Reviews",
    tags: [
      "transparent labs mass gainer protein powder",
      "transparent labs mass gainer",
      "transparent labs mass gainer review",
      "transparent labs weight gainer",
      "transparent labs mass gainer nutrition facts"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{
    text: "See Our Top Weight Gain Picks",
    link: "/best-protein-powder-for-weight-gain/",
  }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <ArticleHeader kicker={"Brand Review"} badge={"Label-Checked"} author={author} dates={dates} mobileAd={false}>
      <Fragment slot="title">Transparent Labs Mass Gainer Protein Powder Review</Fragment>
      Transparent Labs Mass Gainer is a smaller, cleaner-label gainer: about 770 calories instead of 1,250. Here is what is in it, whether the Informed Choice claim holds up, what it costs and who it suits.
    </ArticleHeader>

    <TableOfContents>
      <a href="#short-answer">Short Answer</a>
      <a href="#top-picks">The Products</a>
      <a href="#whats-in-it">What Is in It</a>
      <a href="#third-party-tested">Third-Party Testing</a>
      <a href="#calories">Why 770 Calories</a>
      <a href="#cost">Cost per 25 g</a>
      <a href="#buyer-feedback">Taste and Mixing</a>
      <a href="#vs-other-gainers">vs Other Gainers</a>
      <a href="#healthy">Is It Healthy?</a>
      <a href="#who-should-buy">Who Should Buy It</a>
      <a href="#mistakes">Common Mistakes</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </TableOfContents>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          Transparent Labs Mass Gainer is one of the better-built gainers on a label: per the Chocolate Glaze panel, two scoops give 770 calories, 53 g of grass-fed whey protein and 3 g of creatine, sweetened with stevia, and the brand says it is Informed Choice certified. What changes the verdict is how many calories you need. Below we cover the label, testing, cost per 25 g and the health trade-offs.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Transparent Labs Mass Gainer Protein Powder: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            Transparent Labs Mass Gainer is a good gainer for lifters who want a moderate calorie boost from a short, stevia-sweetened label, and it is third-party tested: the brand says every batch goes to an outside lab and that the product is Informed Choice certified. Per the Chocolate Glaze label at the time of writing, two scoops give 770 calories, 53 g of protein, 110 g of carbohydrate, 15 g of fat and 3 g of creatine. At the $79.99 we saw on Amazon, that is about $2.52 per 25 g of protein.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Buy it if</strong> you want roughly 750 extra calories a day, care about certification and dislike sucralose. <strong>Skip it if</strong> you need 1,200-plus calories from one shake, want the cheapest calories possible, are watching saturated fat, or have diabetes or kidney disease and have not cleared a gainer with your doctor. Our <a href="/best-protein-powder-for-weight-gain/">weight gain protein guide</a> ranks it against the rest of the category.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-4">By the Numbers (Chocolate Glaze label)</p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-center">
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">770</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Calories per 2 scoops</p>
